g how they might punish them, because of the people: for all men glorified God for that which was done.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRFor the man was above forty years old, on whom this miracle of healing was shewed.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAnd being let go, they went to their own company, and reported all that the chief priests and elders had said unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ³And when they heard that, they lifted up their voice to God with one accord, and said, Lord, thou art God, which hast made heaven, and earth, and the sea, and all that in them is:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ0Who by the mouth of thy servant David hast said,¦layout ‚¤text¹Why did the heathen rage,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ#And the people imagine vain things?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ The kings of the earth stood up,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And the rulers were gathered together¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ)Against the Lord, and against his Christ.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªFor of a truth against thy holy child Jesus, whom thou hast anointed, both Herod, and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles, and the people of Israel, were gathered together,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKfor to do whatsoever thy hand and thy counsel determined before to be done.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd now, Lord, behold their threatenings: and grant unto thy servants, that with all boldness they may speak thy word,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsby stretching forth thine hand to heal; and that signs and wonders may be done by the name of thy holy child Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®And when they had prayed, the place was shaken where they were assembled together; and they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and they spake the word of God with boldness.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse#¦verses”„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼And the multitude of them that believed were of one heart and of one soul: neither said any of them that ought of the things which he possessed was his own; but they had all things common.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAnd with great power gave the apostles witness of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus: and great grace was upon them all.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸNeither was there any among them that lacked: for as many as were possessors of lands or houses sold them, and brought the prices of the things that were sold,¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙland laid them down at the apostles' feet: and distribution was made unto every man according as he had need.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book+§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse%¦verses’„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”And Joses, who by the apostles was surnamed Barnabas, (which is, being interpreted, The son of consolation,) a Levite, and of the country of Cyprus,¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOhaving land, sold it, and brought the money, and laid it at the apostles' feet.¦layout ªlast_verse%